What is a Promissory Note?
A Promissory Note is a legal document used to record the terms of a loan between a lender and borrower. It clearly states the loan amount, repayment schedule, interest rate, due dates, late fees, collateral terms, and consequences of non-payment.
A professionally drafted Promissory Note helps both parties understand their rights and obligations. Whether lending money to a friend, family member, business, or private borrower, this document creates written proof of the arrangement.

